                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "vlm":</h3><p><b>VLM</b>, or <em>Very Low Mass</em>, is a trademark of Audix Corporation. VLM is a feature of the company&#8217;s D-series microphones. A low-mass diaphragm mounted to the moving-coil cartridge, in combination with an air suspension system, &#8220;allows the outer wall of the diaphragm to react to sound waves, harmonics and sub-harmonics quicker than other mics. The result is a faster, more precise sampling of the original sound.&#8221;</p><p>Audix at one time promoted VLM in conjunction with &#8220;Sub-Impulse Technology,&#8221; which was &#8220;designed specifically to achieve the true 3-dimensional sound of instruments.&#8221;</p>
